<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Robustness and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-stability.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Where device-independent analyses model global noise levels (see
e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>), CBL introduces a *local* differential notion of
stability: the sensitivity <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dS/dp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dS/dp</annotation></semantics></math> of a witness to infinitesimal flips.
This supports perturbative continuity and worst-case guarantees
(Prop. <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3 (Worst-case bound). ‣ 13.3 Adversarial bounded power ‣ 13 Noise Models and Robustness Guarantees ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), tying robustness directly to admissible
perturbation budgets.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Temporal and causal extensions.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Standard frameworks are static; CBL’s fold/lag operators encode time-correlated or causally
ordered measurements without collapsing contexts (Axiom A3).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Complexity and algorithmic parallels.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CBL interprets contextual constraints as clauses in a curved Boolean algebra. Flat limits
reduce to classical SAT; curvature induces geometrically guided pruning rules, bridging
contextuality and algorithmic constraint satisfaction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Provenance and auditability.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CBL formalizes tamper-evident certificates summarizing noise bounds and fold/lag
outcomes, grounding reproducibility in the same <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-stability theory.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Assumptions and Dependency Matrix</h2>

<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Goal.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We make <em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">every</em> assumption explicit, state the physical motivation, and record which results depend on which assumptions.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Axiom A1: Measurement independence)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Data acquisition choices are statistically independent of the latent variables affecting outcomes (no “setting–hidden-variable” correlation).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Axiom A2: <math id="Thmdefinition2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-bounded perturbations)<span id="Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Admissible perturbations act as flips or deformations whose total variation on any face statistic is bounded by <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> per unit mass (formalized in Sec. <a href="#S13" title="13 Noise Models and Robustness Guarantees ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Axiom A3: Mixing for folds)<span id="Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When folding or stacking runs, windowed aggregates satisfy a mild mixing condition (e.g., <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-mixing) so empirical means converge and permutation-based nulls are well-defined.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Axiom A4: Context-preserving instrumentation)<span id="Thmdefinition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Measurement contexts are well-specified; changing a context is recorded as such (no silent cross-talk that re-labels contexts).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Axiom A5: Finite-moment regularity)<span id="Thmdefinition5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">All random variables used in estimators have finite second moments; covariance matrices used in bounds are non-singular on the support considered (degenerate cases handled separately).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dependency matrix.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Dependency matrix. ‣ 4 Assumptions and Dependency Matrix ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> lists which results use which axioms (a filled dot means “used essentially”; an open circle “used for convenience, removable with work”).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
