</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Non-generic/degenerate cases.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When parameters approach boundaries (e.g., <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}\!\to\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}\!\to\!0</annotation></semantics></math>, singular covariance, or
zero-count bins), our statements remain valid by continuity or are restated with weakened
constants; see Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Expanded Proofs and Boundary-Case Analysis ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> for explicit limits and counterexamples.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Curved Boolean Logic: Semantics</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite set of propositional variables.
A <em id="S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">context system</em> is a finite family <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\{C_{i}\}_{i\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\{C_{i}\}_{i\in I}</annotation></semantics></math> of nonempty subsets <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>
such that each <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math> appears in at least one <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Intuitively, each <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is a set of jointly testable variables.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local and global valuations)<span id="Thmdefinition6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A <em id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">local valuation</em> on context <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a Boolean assignment <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{C}:C\to\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{C}:C\to\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A family <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\ell_{C}\}_{C\in\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\ell_{C}\}_{C\in\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">compatible</em> if for all <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C,C^{\prime}\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C,C^{\prime}\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{C}|_{C\cap C^{\prime}}=\ell_{C^{\prime}}|_{C\cap C^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{C}|_{C\cap C^{\prime}}=\ell_{C^{\prime}}|_{C\cap C^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A <em id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">global valuation</em> is <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:V\to\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:V\to\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> restricting to each <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Curvature.</h5>

<div id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We say <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V,\mathcal{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V,\mathcal{C})</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">flat</em> if every compatible family admits a global valuation;
otherwise it is <em id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">curved</em>.
Curvature measures the obstruction to extending local truths to a global ledger.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Sheaf semantics</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Ctx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖢𝗍𝗑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Ctx}</annotation></semantics></math> be the poset category of contexts ordered by inclusion.
Define a presheaf <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}(C)=\{0,1\}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}(C)=\{0,1\}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and, for <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subseteq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subseteq C</annotation></semantics></math>,
restriction maps <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{CD}:\mathcal{F}(C)\to\mathcal{F}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{CD}:\mathcal{F}(C)\to\mathcal{F}(D)</annotation></semantics></math> by restriction of functions.
A compatible family is a matching family; a global section is <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{F}(V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{F}(V)</annotation></semantics></math> restricting to each <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Curvature functional)<span id="Thmdefinition7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A curvature functional is any map <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa:(V,\mathcal{C})\mapsto\mathbb{N}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa:(V,\mathcal{C})\mapsto\mathbb{N}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=0</annotation></semantics></math> iff every compatible family admits a global section,
and <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is monotone under context refinement.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Cohomological view</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following Abramsky <em id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">et al.</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>,
consider the nerve of the cover <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and the presheaf <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> assigning <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1\}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1\}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> under XOR.
A compatible family is a <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>-cocycle; a global section exists iff its class is trivial in <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\mathsf{Ctx},\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖢𝗍𝗑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\mathsf{Ctx},\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We may therefore set</p>
<table id="S5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(V,\mathcal{C})\;=\;\mathrm{rank}\big(H^{1}(\mathsf{Ctx},\mathcal{A})\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖢𝗍𝗑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(V,\mathcal{C})\;=\;\mathrm{rank}\big(H^{1}(\mathsf{Ctx},\mathcal{A})\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Exclusivity-graph semantics</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define the compatibility hypergraph <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> with hyperedges <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For overlaps, duplicate variables as <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{(C)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{(C)}</annotation></semantics></math> and require <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{(C)}=v^{(C^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{(C)}=v^{(C^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in C\cap C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in C\cap C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Curvature corresponds to cycles whose joint constraints forbid a global assignment.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Equivalence of semantics)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For finite context systems, sheaf semantics and exclusivity-hypergraph semantics are equivalent:
a compatible family admits a global section iff the exclusivity formulation admits an assignment consistent on overlaps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Sketch.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Quotient <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{C\in\mathcal{C}}\{0,1\}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{C\in\mathcal{C}}\{0,1\}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> by overlap equalities; the quotient is isomorphic to global sections of <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Conversely, any global section induces equal copies across contexts.
Obstructions correspond to nontrivial <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-cocycles (sheaf) or chordless cycles (graph).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>Context lattice diagram</h3>

