</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Proof Theory</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We develop a context-sequent calculus to reason in CBL.
Sequents are annotated with contexts: <math id="S7.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma\vdash_{C}\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\vdash_{C}\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> means within context <math id="S7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, from assumptions <math id="S7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, infer <math id="S7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1 </span>Local rules</h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Within a fixed context <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, inference is standard propositional sequent calculus.
Weakening, contraction, cut, and introduction rules for <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\land,\lor,\lnot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∧</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∨</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>¬</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\land,\lor,\lnot</annotation></semantics></math> apply to variables in <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> only.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.2 </span>Overlap rules</h3>

<div id="S7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Contexts overlap; we allow transport and consistency rules:</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S7.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Gamma\vdash_{C}\psi\quad\mathrm{Vars}(\psi)\subseteq C\cap C^{\prime}}{\Gamma\vdash_{C^{\prime}}\psi}\quad(\mathrm{OVL})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>Vars</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>OVL</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Gamma\vdash_{C}\psi\quad\mathrm{Vars}(\psi)\subseteq C\cap C^{\prime}}{\Gamma\vdash_{C^{\prime}}\psi}\quad(\mathrm{OVL})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S7.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Gamma,\psi\vdash_{C}\bot\quad\Gamma,\lnot\psi\vdash_{C^{\prime}}\bot}{\Gamma\vdash_{C\cup C^{\prime}}\bot}\quad(\mathrm{CONS})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo rspace="0em">⊢</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⊥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo rspace="0em">⊢</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em">⊥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo rspace="0em">⊢</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">⊥</mo></mrow></mfrac><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>CONS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Gamma,\psi\vdash_{C}\bot\quad\Gamma,\lnot\psi\vdash_{C^{\prime}}\bot}{\Gamma\vdash_{C\cup C^{\prime}}\bot}\quad(\mathrm{CONS})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These rules enforce that overlaps agree and contradictions on overlaps propagate globally.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.3 </span>Soundness</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Soundness)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma\vdash_{C}\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\vdash_{C}\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is derivable, then every local valuation <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{C}\models\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>⊧</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{C}\models\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>.
With the overlap and consistency rules (OVL, CONS), derivability is sound with respect
to the sheaf semantics introduced in Sec. <a href="#S5" title="5 Curved Boolean Logic: Semantics ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Sketch.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Local rules coincide with the classical propositional sequent calculus and are therefore
sound. For (OVL), if <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma\vdash_{C}\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\vdash_{C}\psi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Vars}(\psi)\subseteq C\cap C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Vars</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Vars}(\psi)\subseteq C\cap C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, then
compatibility of local valuations ensures <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{C^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{C^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> agrees on the overlap, hence <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>
also holds in <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. For (CONS), if <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma,\psi\vdash_{C}\bot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo rspace="0em">⊢</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">⊥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma,\psi\vdash_{C}\bot</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S7.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma,\neg\psi\vdash_{C^{\prime}}\bot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo rspace="0em">⊢</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em">⊥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma,\neg\psi\vdash_{C^{\prime}}\bot</annotation></semantics></math>, any global assignment extending both contexts
would contradict itself on <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\cup C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\cup C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.4 </span>Flat-limit conservativity</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Flat-limit conservativity)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(V,C)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(V,C)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma\vdash_{C}\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\vdash_{C}\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is derivable in CBL if and only if
the same sequent is derivable in classical propositional logic.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Sketch.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="S7.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(V,C)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(V,C)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, every compatible local family admits a global valuation; thus
CBL derivability coincides with Boolean derivability.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.5 </span>Proof trees</h3>

<figure id="S7.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S7.F3.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:310.5pt;height:33.8pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-142.3pt,15.5pt) scale(0.521688388610253,0.521688388610253) ;"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S7.F3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="89.61" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 823.55 89.61" width="823.55"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,89.61) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(158.48,0) translate(0,78.85)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -57.42 -4.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.27em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="115.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Global valuation</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -96.32 -43.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="50.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Clause A</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -17.44 -9.69 L -50.74 -28.19"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-width="0.76822pt" transform="matrix(-0.8742 -0.48557 0.48557 -0.8742 -48.78 -27.1)"><path d="M 4.88 0 L 1.72 1.17 L 2.51 0 L 1.72 -1.17 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -25.19 -43.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="50.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Clause B</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -9.69 L 0 -26.1"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-width="0.76822pt" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -23.86)"><path d="M 4.88 0 L 1.72 1.17 L 2.51 0 L 1.72 -1.17 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 45.59 -43.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.95em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="50.56"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Clause C</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 17.44 -9.69 L 50.74 -28.19"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-width="0.76822pt" transform="matrix(0.8742 -0.48557 0.48557 0.8742 48.78 -27.1)"><path d="M 4.88 0 L 1.72 1.17 L 2.51 0 L 1.72 -1.17 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 401.84 -3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="136.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No global valuation</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 366.42 -48.64)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 18.54)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.51)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.86em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="49.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Context </span><math id="S7.F3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 18.54)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 7.1 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="50.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Clause A</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 449.97 -11.04 L 428 -23.24"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-width="0.76822pt" transform="matrix(-0.87422 -0.48553 0.48553 -0.87422 429.96 -22.15)"><path d="M 4.88 0 L 1.72 1.17 L 2.51 0 L 1.72 -1.17 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 437.28 -48.64)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 18.54)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.51)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.86em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="49.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Context </span><math id="S7.F3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 18.54)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 7.36 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="50.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Clause B</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 469.84 -11.04 L 469.84 -21.15"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-width="0.76822pt" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 469.84 -18.91)"><path d="M 4.88 0 L 1.72 1.17 L 2.51 0 L 1.72 -1.17 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 502.12 -48.64)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 18.54)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.51)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 6.04 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.86em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="49.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Context </span><math id="S7.F3.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 18.54)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="77.54"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Contradiction</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 489.7 -11.04 L 511.68 -23.24"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-width="0.76822pt" transform="matrix(0.87422 -0.48553 0.48553 0.87422 509.72 -22.15)"><path d="M 4.88 0 L 1.72 1.17 L 2.51 0 L 1.72 -1.17 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -153.86 -70.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.15em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="309.1"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Flat proof tree:</span><span id="S7.F3.pic1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> global valuation ensures consistency.</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 279.22 -71.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="381.96"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S7.F3.pic1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Curved proof tree:</span><span id="S7.F3.pic1.15" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> local branches exist but global valuation fails.</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S7.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S7.F3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Flat vs. curved proof trees.
In flat cases, a global valuation ensures consistency;
in curved cases, local branches exist but no global valuation exists, producing a structural contradiction.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>CBL-SAT and Complexity</h2>

<section id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scope and claims.</h5>

<div id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We make <em id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">no</em> blanket claim of asymptotic speedups for arbitrary SAT. Our contributions are:
(i) structural reductions showing how curvature/overlap parameters control branching and pruning in certain families,
(ii) formal bounds connecting runtime to curvature rank under A1–A5,
(iii) empirical evidence on structured benchmarks.
We highlight open problems where tighter worst-case bounds or lower bounds may hold.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 9</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmdefinition9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CBL-SAT</span>)<span id="Thmdefinition9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Instance: a context system <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V,\mathcal{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V,\mathcal{C})</annotation></semantics></math> and a set of clauses <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>,
each clause <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> attached to a context <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\phi)\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\phi)\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Question: does there exist a compatible family <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\ell_{C}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\ell_{C}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{C(\phi)}\models\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊧</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{C(\phi)}\models\phi</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>?</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.1 </span>Basic properties</h3>

<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(NP-membership)<span id="Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CBL-SAT<span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in</annotation></semantics></math> NP.
Certificate: local assignments <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Verification: check local clause satisfaction and overlap equalities in polynomial time.</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Flat limit)<span id="Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CBL-SAT</span> reduces to SAT by the global valuation extending all <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.2 </span>Hardness</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CBL-SAT<span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is NP-complete.</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Sketch.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Membership: by certificate verification.
Hardness: reduce SAT to CBL-SAT by taking a single context <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=V</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus CBL-SAT inherits NP-completeness.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.3 </span>Tractable subclasses</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Treewidth)<span id="Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If the context hypergraph has bounded treewidth and each clause respects a bag,
<span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CBL-SAT</span> is solvable in polynomial time by dynamic programming.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Sketch.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Maintain tables of partial assignments on bags.
Propagate overlaps through introduce/forget/join nodes.
Runtime <math id="S8.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(|\Phi|\cdot 2^{O(w)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(|\Phi|\cdot 2^{O(w)})</annotation></semantics></math> with treewidth <math id="S8.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.4 </span>Parameterized complexity</h3>

<div id="S8.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Parameters of interest:</p>
<ul id="S8.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Maximum overlap size <math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>: fixed <math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> yields polynomial overlap checks.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Number of curved cores: bounded number allows branching then flattening.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Curvature rank <math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>: small <math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> may yield FPT algorithms.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.5 </span>Counting</h3>

<div id="S8.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">#CBL-SAT</span>: count compatible families.
This is #P-complete, extending #SAT.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S8.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S8.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S8.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Placeholder: counting compatible families.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S8.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S8.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S8.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Instance</td>
<td id="S8.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt">Vars</td>
<td id="S8.T4.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt">Contexts</td>
<td id="S8.T4.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"># Compatible families</td></tr>
<tr id="S8.T4.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
