</figure>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.2 </span>Worked pruning trace</h3>

<div id="S9.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On KCBS (pentagon), suppose <math id="S9.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}=\mathrm{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}=\mathrm{T}</annotation></semantics></math> chosen.
Propagation forces <math id="S9.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{2}=\mathrm{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{2}=\mathrm{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S9.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3}=\mathrm{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3}=\mathrm{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, etc.
Eventually <math id="S9.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{5}=\mathrm{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{5}=\mathrm{T}</annotation></semantics></math> forces <math id="S9.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}=\mathrm{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}=\mathrm{F}</annotation></semantics></math> via overlap.
Contradiction found earlier than in flat SAT, pruning entire branch.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.3 </span>Toy overlap code</h3>

<div id="S9.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para"><pre id="S9.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
def check_overlap(lC, lCp, overlap_vars):
    """Return True if assignments lC and lCp agree on overlap."""
    for v in overlap_vars:
        if lC[v] != lCp[v]:
            return False
    return True
</pre>
</div>
</section>
