<section id="S17.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summary.</h5>

<div id="S17.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adhering to this protocol guarantees that every visual claim is statistically auditable and reproducible,
satisfying the quantitative-transparency standards expected in quantum-foundations and experimental-physics review processes.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S18" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">18 </span>Reproducible Analysis Notebook (Colab-Ready)</h2>

<section id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Artifact and availability.</h5>

<div id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The notebook <span id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">cbl_perm_bh_notebook.ipynb</span> and parameter file
<span id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">params_example.json</span> are included as <em id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ancillary files</em> with this arXiv submission.
Readers can obtain them from the paper’s arXiv page via
<em id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Other formats</em> <math id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Download all files</em>; ancillary items appear in the source bundle.
(Ancillary URLs follow the pattern <span id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">https://arxiv.org/src/&lt;arXivID&gt;/anc/&lt;filename&gt;</span> once the ID is assigned.)</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Purpose.</h5>

<div id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section binds the statistical procedures of Sec. <a href="#S20" title="20 Statistical Procedures, Multiple-Testing Control, and Reproducibility ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> to an executable, self-contained notebook that generates all standardized figures in Sec. <a href="#S17" title="17 Figure Standards and Visualization Protocol ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>. The notebook implements permutation-based empirical <math id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values, Benjamini–Hochberg FDR control, and block-wise permutations aligned with Axiom A3.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Artifacts.</h5>

<div id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a Colab-ready notebook (<span id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">cbl_perm_bh_notebook.ipynb</span>) and an example parameter file. Running the notebook end-to-end produces the following figures and files:</p>
<ul id="S18.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S18.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S18.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">figs/epsilon_stability.pdf</span> — <math id="S18.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-stability curve (finite-difference <math id="S18.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dS/dp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dS/dp</annotation></semantics></math> approximation).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S18.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S18.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">figs/fold_lag_scan.pdf</span> — observed folded statistic with permutation-null band.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S18.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S18.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">figs/fold_lag_scan_qvals.pdf</span> — corrected <math id="S18.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-values (BH-FDR).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S18.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S18.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">figs/power_grid.pdf</span> — power/robustness grid over <math id="S18.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Determinism and parameters.</h5>

<div id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All random draws use a fixed seed exposed in the top-level parameter cell. Captions must include <math id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w,s,B,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w,s,B,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">seed</span>, matching the standards in Sec. <a href="#S17" title="17 Figure Standards and Visualization Protocol ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Synthetic vs. real data.</h5>

<div id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By default, the notebook generates synthetic AR(1)-modulated streams with flip rate <math id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, creating two alternating contexts to exercise fold/lag scans. To use real data, replace the generator with a loader that returns:</p>
<table id="S18.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S18.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{t},y_{t})_{t=1}^{N},\quad x_{t}\in\{0,1,\dots\},\;y_{t}\in\{0,1\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{t},y_{t})_{t=1}^{N},\quad x_{t}\in\{0,1,\dots\},\;y_{t}\in\{0,1\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and keep the folding/permutation steps unchanged to preserve the validity of the permutation null.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Execution protocol.</h5>

<div id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The computational artifact (<span id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">cbl_perm_bh_notebook.ipynb</span>) reproduces all figures and statistics in this paper without external dependencies beyond NumPy/Matplotlib. To execute:</p>
<ol id="S18.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S18.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S18.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Open <span id="S18.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">cbl_perm_bh_notebook.ipynb</span> in a Python 3 / Colab environment.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S18.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S18.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Run all cells. The notebook is self-contained (no internet access required).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S18.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S18.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The notebook writes the following PDFs into <span id="S18.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">figs/</span>:</p>
<ul id="S18.I2.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">epsilon_stability.pdf</span>  <math id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Fig. <a href="#S17.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 17.2 Example 1 — 𝜀-Stability Curve ‣ 17 Figure Standards and Visualization Protocol ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fold_lag_scan.pdf</span>  <math id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Fig. <a href="#S17.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ 17.3 Example 2 — Folded Lag Scan ‣ 17 Figure Standards and Visualization Protocol ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">power_grid.pdf</span>  <math id="S18.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Fig. <a href="#S17.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ 17.4 Example 3 — Power and Robustness Grid ‣ 17 Figure Standards and Visualization Protocol ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Outputs.</h5>

<div id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The generated PDFs correspond one-to-one to the figures cited above and are produced with the exact seeds and parameters stated in their captions. The notebook also saves intermediate arrays (test statistics, permutation null bands, <math id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-values) to temporary files to facilitate audit and reuse.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Environment and determinism.</h5>

<div id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All runs are deterministic given the exposed seed. The artifact specifies package versions and parameters (see Table <a href="#S20.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Reproducibility checklist. ‣ 20 Statistical Procedures, Multiple-Testing Control, and Reproducibility ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>); no GPU or special hardware is required. Real-data use follows the same interface as the synthetic generator described earlier, preserving the validity of the permutation null.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px9" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Alignment with Sec. <a href="#S20" title="20 Statistical Procedures, Multiple-Testing Control, and Reproducibility ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>.</h5>

<div id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The implementation corresponds exactly to Algorithm <a href="#algorithm4" title="In Null bands for figures. ‣ 20 Statistical Procedures, Multiple-Testing Control, and Reproducibility ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and uses block permutations respecting Axiom A3 (mixing). The shaded null band uses the <math id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.5</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="97.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>97.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">97.5</annotation></semantics></math> percentile envelope over <math id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> permutations. BH-FDR controls the discovery rate across windows at level <math id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px10" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">File manifest (supplement).</h5>

<div id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We include a short README and example parameter file:</p>
<ul id="S18.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S18.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S18.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">README_CBL_Notebook.txt</span> — run instructions and file map.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S18.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S18.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">params_example.json</span> — canonical parameter values for quick runs.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px11" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Compliance.</h5>

<div id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures produced by the notebook satisfy the single-plot rule, include null bands and corrected <math id="S18.SS0.SSS0.Px11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-values, and record all parameters required by Table <a href="#S17.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 17.5 Compliance Checklist ‣ 17 Figure Standards and Visualization Protocol ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Table <a href="#S20.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Reproducibility checklist. ‣ 20 Statistical Procedures, Multiple-Testing Control, and Reproducibility ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S19" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">19 </span>Validated Figures from Reproducible Notebook</h2>

<section id="S19.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Source.</h5>

<div id="S19.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S19.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All figures in this section are generated directly by the Colab notebook
<span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">cbl_perm_bh_notebook.ipynb</span> using parameters listed in
<span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">params_example.json</span>. The notebook and parameter file are provided as ancillary
files with this arXiv submission (see Sec. <a href="#S18" title="18 Reproducible Analysis Notebook (Colab-Ready) ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>). Each caption
reports the exact <math id="S19.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w,s,B,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w,s,B,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="S19.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">seed</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S20" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">20 </span>Statistical Procedures, Multiple-Testing Control, and Reproducibility</h2>

<section id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Permutation-based empirical <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values.</h5>

<div id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any scalar test statistic <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> computed from labels/outcomes, we build an empirical null by <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> random permutations of the relevant labels within admissible blocks (respecting the fold windows). The one-sided empirical <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value is</p>
<table id="S20.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S20.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathrm{emp}}=\frac{1+\#\{b:T^{(b)}\geq T_{\mathrm{obs}}\}}{1+B}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>emp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>obs</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{emp}}=\frac{1+\#\{b:T^{(b)}\geq T_{\mathrm{obs}}\}}{1+B}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sliding scans and FDR control.</h5>

<div id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When scanning <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> windows and/or thresholds, we control the false discovery rate with Benjamini–Hochberg at level <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> on the vector <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{\mathrm{emp}}^{(m)})_{m=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>emp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{\mathrm{emp}}^{(m)})_{m=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, declaring discoveries for all <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="S20.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S20.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{emp}}^{(m)}\leq\frac{k_{m}}{M}\alpha,\quad k_{m}=\max\{k:p_{(k)}\leq k\alpha/M\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>emp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{emp}}^{(m)}\leq\frac{k_{m}}{M}\alpha,\quad k_{m}=\max\{k:p_{(k)}\leq k\alpha/M\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Null bands for figures.</h5>

<div id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any curve, we display the <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[2.5,97.5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>97.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2.5,97.5]</annotation></semantics></math> percentile envelope from the permutation distribution as a shaded band. Report both the corrected <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-value and an effect size (e.g., standardized difference).</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm4" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span>Folded-scan with permutation null and BH-FDR</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm4.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm4.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm4.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Data stream <math id="algorithm4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{t},y_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{t},y_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>; window <math id="algorithm4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>; step <math id="algorithm4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>; statistic <math id="algorithm4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>; permutations <math id="algorithm4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>; FDR <math id="algorithm4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm4.4.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm4.4.2.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.4.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            Form window <math id="algorithm4.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{\ell}=\{t:t\in[t_{0}+(\ell-1)s,\,t_{0}+(\ell-1)s+w)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\ell}=\{t:t\in[t_{0}+(\ell-1)s,\,t_{0}+(\ell-1)s+w)\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            Compute <math id="algorithm4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=T(W_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=T(W_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm4.4.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm4.4.5.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm4.4.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.4.5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            Permute labels/outcomes within blocks respecting A3; compute <math id="algorithm4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{(b)}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{(b)}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm4.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\ell}\leftarrow\frac{1+\#\{b:T^{(b)}_{\ell}\geq T_{\ell}\}}{1+B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\ell}\leftarrow\frac{1+\#\{b:T^{(b)}_{\ell}\geq T_{\ell}\}}{1+B}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
            Apply BH at level <math id="algorithm4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="algorithm4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{\ell}\}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{\ell}\}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain discoveries <math id="algorithm4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>; return <math id="algorithm4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(T_{\ell},p_{\ell})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(T_{\ell},p_{\ell})\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algorithm4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
