<section id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Provenance certificate (tamper-evident).</h5>

<div id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each run emits a machine-readable certificate with identity &amp; scope, randomness provenance, <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbation parameters, fold/lag statistics (with corrected <math id="S20.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-values), and cryptographic digests of logs (see supplement schema).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S21" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">21 </span>Empirical Results (Placeholder)</h2>

<div id="S21.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S21.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section will present quantitative benchmarks once empirical data is available.
Currently, placeholders illustrate the intended evaluations:</p>
</div>
<div id="S21.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S21.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S21.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S21.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S21.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Synthetic KCBS and Mermin families of increasing size, measuring pruning rates and runtime scaling.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S21.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S21.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S21.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Random CNF instances with planted context structures, showing difference between flat and curved cases.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S21.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S21.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S21.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Industrial SAT competition benchmarks (crafted, random, and industrial tracks) with context grouping policy.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="S21.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Synthetic families</h3>

<div id="S21.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S21.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures in Sec. <a href="#S9" title="9 Solver: Curvature-Aware Backtracking ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> include placeholders: scaling with number of contexts, runtime vs curvature rank <math id="S21.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, UNSAT detection depth, and learned overlap cuts.
Real data will replace these with reproducible experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S21.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">SAT competition benchmarks</h3>

<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(SAT competition evaluation)<span id="Thmremark1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Evaluation will include SAT competition suites with a reproducible context-construction policy:
clauses grouped by overlap or module boundaries.
CBL-hybrid runs integrated into CDCL solvers will ensure flat instances incur near-zero overhead,
while curved instances benefit from earlier refutations.
Metrics: wall-clock time, node counts, learned overlap cuts, reproducibility with fixed seeds.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S21.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Industrial placeholder</h3>

<div id="S21.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S21.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The processor pipeline sketch in Sec. <a href="#S6" title="6 Canonical Curved Examples ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> illustrates one case study.
Future work will include larger hardware verification and software model checking instances,
measuring whether curvature-aware pruning yields practical runtime benefits.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S22" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">22 </span>Receipt-Checked CBL Certificates and Constant-Gap Detectors</h2>

<section id="S22.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Motivation.</h5>

<div id="S22.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond foundational interest, CBL enables an operational primitive:
<em id="S22.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">receipt-checked contextual certificates</em> aggregated coherently to
yield a <em id="S22.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">constant gap</em> between empty and non-empty cases of a search
property. The mechanism is the same phase-per-face effect behind
<math id="S22.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{CBL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>CBL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{CBL}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Sec. <a href="#S23" title="23 Topological holonomy invariant in CBL ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>): each enabled
<em id="S22.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">contextual face</em> adds a fixed phase contribution, while the
geometry-dependent remainder decays like <math id="S22.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/L)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S22.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">22.1 </span>Witness modules and certificate discipline</h3>

<div id="S22.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <em id="S22.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">witness module</em> <math id="S22.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> monitors a small clause/window and opens
its gate <em id="S22.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">iff</em> a monotone NGCC cut is provably violated under the
current wiring. “Provably” means:</p>
<ol id="S22.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.3em;">
<li id="S22.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S22.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">build the local feasibility LP for the window with the NGCC cut,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S22.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S22.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">if infeasible, extract the dual (Farkas) certificate, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S22.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S22.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">re-verify the dual in exact/rational arithmetic.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S22.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Only then does <math id="S22.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> contribute a marked amplitude <math id="S22.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}e^{i\phi_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}e^{i\phi_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>
to a common rail; otherwise it contributes 0. Gate openings are
<em id="S22.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">receipt-checked</em>. Modules are placed on <em id="S22.SS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">disjoint</em> wire sets,
so their phases <math id="S22.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent apart from bounded jitter.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S22.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">22.2 </span>Holonomy split and constant term</h3>

<div id="S22.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S22.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a loop enclosing <math id="S22.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\Sigma_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\Sigma_{L})</annotation></semantics></math> contextual faces with boundary length <math id="S22.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the holonomy decomposition reviewed in Sec. <a href="#S23.SS1" title="23.1 Holonomy decomposition ‣ 23 Topological holonomy invariant in CBL ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23.1</span></a>
(see also Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Expanded Proofs and Boundary-Case Analysis ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>), the per-edge holonomy splits into a geometric tail
and a topological term:</p>
<table id="S22.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S22.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{L}\!\oint_{\gamma_{L}}\!A\;=\;\underbrace{\frac{1}{L}\!\oint_{\gamma_{L}}\!A_{\mathrm{geom}}}_{O(L^{-1})}\;+\;\theta_{0}\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}},\qquad\rho_{\mathrm{face}}:=\lim_{L\to\infty}\frac{F(\Sigma_{L})}{L}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>geom</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{L}\!\oint_{\gamma_{L}}\!A\;=\;\underbrace{\frac{1}{L}\!\oint_{\gamma_{L}}\!A_{\mathrm{geom}}}_{O(L^{-1})}\;+\;\theta_{0}\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}},\qquad\rho_{\mathrm{face}}:=\lim_{L\to\infty}\frac{F(\Sigma_{L})}{L}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S22.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus the per-edge marked phase has a size-independent component <math id="S22.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}}</annotation></semantics></math>
plus an <math id="S22.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/L)</annotation></semantics></math> tail. After one calibration (Sec. <a href="#S23.SS1" title="23.1 Holonomy decomposition ‣ 23 Topological holonomy invariant in CBL ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23.1</span></a>),
we identify <math id="S22.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{CBL}}=|\theta_{0}|\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}}/(2\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>CBL</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{CBL}}=|\theta_{0}|\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}}/(2\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S22.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">22.3 </span>Coherent fan-in bound (receipt-checked)</h3>

<div id="S22.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S22.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of modules that open under certificate discipline.
With a background <math id="S22.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> phase-aligned at readout,
the marked amplitude is
<math id="S22.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\max}=|b|+\big|\sum_{j\in J}a_{0}e^{i\phi_{j}}\big|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\max}=|b|+\big|\sum_{j\in J}a_{0}e^{i\phi_{j}}\big|.</annotation></semantics></math>
If <math id="S22.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\phi_{j}|\leq\sigma\leq 0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\phi_{j}|\leq\sigma\leq 0.15</annotation></semantics></math> rad and at most an <math id="S22.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\rm cert}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>cert</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\rm cert}</annotation></semantics></math>
fraction of opens are erroneous, then</p>
<table id="S22.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S22.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\max}\;\geq\;|b|\;+\;a_{0}\,|J|(\cos\sigma-\sin\sigma)\;-\;O(\epsilon_{\rm cert}\,a_{0}|J|)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>cert</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\max}\;\geq\;|b|\;+\;a_{0}\,|J|(\cos\sigma-\sin\sigma)\;-\;O(\epsilon_{\rm cert}\,a_{0}|J|),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S22.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so any configuration that enables <math id="S22.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|J|=\Omega(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|J|=\Omega(1)</annotation></semantics></math> per unit length has a
<em id="S22.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">constant</em> gap at fixed <math id="S22.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0},\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0},\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S22.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">22.4 </span>Where multiplicity comes from</h3>

<div id="S22.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Structured wirings (e.g. Feistelized multiplier windows) provide many
<em id="S22.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">disjoint</em> contextual faces under a false hypothesis. With stride
exceeding the carry radius, we obtain <math id="S22.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\Theta(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\Theta(n)</annotation></semantics></math> disjoint windows over
an <math id="S22.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-bit instance; when the hypothesis is false (e.g. the searched interval
does contain a factor), at least <math id="S22.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\Omega(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\Omega(K)</annotation></semantics></math> violate the local cut,
each with a short dual certificate. Combining (<a href="#S22.E1" title="In 22.3 Coherent fan-in bound (receipt-checked) ‣ 22 Receipt-Checked CBL Certificates and Constant-Gap Detectors ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) with the
holonomy split yields a constant per-edge phase term (the calibrated
<math id="S22.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}\rho_{\mathrm{face}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}\rho_{\mathrm{face}}</annotation></semantics></math>) plus an <math id="S22.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/L)</annotation></semantics></math> tail from geometry.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Binary search via amplitude estimation)<span id="Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If empty intervals produce <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\max}=|b|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\max}=|b|</annotation></semantics></math> and non-empty intervals
produce <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\max}\geq|b|+\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\max}\geq|b|+\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
then interval localization over <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,\sqrt{N}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,\sqrt{N}]</annotation></semantics></math> completes in
<math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log\sqrt{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log\sqrt{N})</annotation></semantics></math> stages with <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{O}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{O}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> amplitude-estimation calls per
stage (precision <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq\Delta/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq\Delta/4</annotation></semantics></math>), for <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{O}(\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{O}(\log N)</annotation></semantics></math> total.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S22.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">22.5 </span>Shor–CFPE as a CBL-monitored control primitive</h3>

<div id="S22.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also adapt the idea to order-finding: Kitaev’s iterative PEA with a
<em id="S22.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">counterfactual</em> controlled <math id="S22.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{a}^{2^{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>a</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{a}^{2^{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> (CF–c<math id="S22.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>). Each round is
guarded by receipt-checked NGCC modules: if the wiring slips into an
inconsistent branch, a certificate is emitted and the round is heralded
for re-try. Under bounded heralded failure probability and small
control-phase error per round, the order is recovered with constant
success probability in <math id="S22.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=2\lceil\log_{2}N\rceil+O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=2\lceil\log_{2}N\rceil+O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> rounds and
expected CF–c<math id="S22.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> calls <math id="S22.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq t/(1-\delta_{\rm ctrl})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ctrl</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq t/(1-\delta_{\rm ctrl})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S22.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Falsifiable checks (no numerology).</h5>

<div id="S22.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S22.I2" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.3em;">
<li id="S22.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S22.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S22.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Single-calibration universality:</span> fix <math id="S22.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on CHSH
(<math id="S22.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\rm face}=1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\rm face}=1/4</annotation></semantics></math>), then verify large-<math id="S22.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> constants on KCBS
(<math id="S22.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/5</annotation></semantics></math>) and the chosen SAT tiling (<math id="S22.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/6</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S22.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2/6</annotation></semantics></math>) match
<math id="S22.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{CBL}}=\frac{|\theta_{0}|}{2\pi}\rho_{\rm face}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>CBL</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{CBL}}=\frac{|\theta_{0}|}{2\pi}\rho_{\rm face}</annotation></semantics></math> within finite-size error.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S22.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S22.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S22.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RG invariance:</span> clause decimation changes only the <math id="S22.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/L</annotation></semantics></math> tail,
not the intercept.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S22.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S22.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S22.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S22.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-probe neutrality:</span> moving the flip positions
changes the slope but leaves the intercept unchanged.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S22.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S22.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S22.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Certificate discipline:</span> measured false-open rate
<math id="S22.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\rm cert}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>cert</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\rm cert}</annotation></semantics></math> must keep the correction in (<a href="#S22.E1" title="In 22.3 Coherent fan-in bound (receipt-checked) ‣ 22 Receipt-Checked CBL Certificates and Constant-Gap Detectors ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) below
the target gap.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S22.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scope note.</h5>

<div id="S22.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section shows that a CBL topological term
(phase per contextual face) yields a size-independent coupling that
<em id="S22.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">can</em> be tied to <math id="S22.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> after one calibration. A calibration-free,
first-principles derivation of <math id="S22.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from CBL axioms remains an open
problem (Sec. <a href="#S23" title="23 Topological holonomy invariant in CBL ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, Open Problem 1).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S22.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Connection to integer factorization.</h5>

<div id="S22.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S22.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The same construction yields a CBL-monitored realization of the
Shor–Kitaev order-finding routine: integer factorization is the special
case where the CF–controlled unitaries implement modular exponentiation,
and receipt-checked CBL modules certify each iteration’s phase
accumulation; see also the broader NGCC framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S23" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">23 </span>Topological holonomy invariant in CBL</h2>

<section id="S23.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summary.</h5>

<div id="S23.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S23.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CBL induces a <math id="S23.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(1)</annotation></semantics></math> connection on the clause complex whose loop holonomy per edge
splits into a geometric tail and a topological term proportional to the density of
contextual faces. This yields a linear law with a size–independent intercept.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S23.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">23.1 </span>Holonomy decomposition</h3>

<div id="S23.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S23.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Write <math id="S23.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=A_{\mathrm{geom}}+\theta_{0}\,\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>geom</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=A_{\mathrm{geom}}+\theta_{0}\,\omega</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S23.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\omega</annotation></semantics></math> supported on faces.
For <math id="S23.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{L}=\partial\Sigma_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{L}=\partial\Sigma_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S23.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S23.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{L}\!\oint_{\gamma_{L}}\!A\;=\;\underbrace{\frac{1}{L}\!\oint_{\gamma_{L}}\!A_{\mathrm{geom}}}_{O(L^{-1})}\;+\;\theta_{0}\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}}(\gamma_{L})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>geom</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{L}\!\oint_{\gamma_{L}}\!A\;=\;\underbrace{\frac{1}{L}\!\oint_{\gamma_{L}}\!A_{\mathrm{geom}}}_{O(L^{-1})}\;+\;\theta_{0}\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}}(\gamma_{L}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S23.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">by discrete Stokes and coarse-graining of <math id="S23.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{geom}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>geom</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{geom}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We use this invariant descriptively; no physical calibration is attempted.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S24" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">24 </span>CBL Constant — CSV-Driven Tables (Families and Mixes)</h2>

<section id="S24.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">24.1 </span>Families (CHSH, KCBS, SAT 1/6, SAT 2/6)</h3>

<figure id="S24.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S24.T8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 8</span>: </span><span id="S24.T8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Appendix (CSV-driven origin; static here): CBL large-<math id="S24.T8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> intercepts <math id="S24.T8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>
after a single CHSH calibration (target <math id="S24.T8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1/137" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>137</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1/137</annotation></semantics></math>). Face density <math id="S24.T8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{face}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{face}}</annotation></semantics></math>
is faces per boundary edge.</span></figcaption>
