<section id="S25" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">25 </span>Open Problems, Conjectures, and Pre-registered Tests</h2>

<section id="S25.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Open Problems.</h5>

<div id="S25.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S25.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S25.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S25.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S25.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S25.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Axiomatically fix the per-face phase <math id="S25.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Show that CBL axioms (Boolean corners, flat limit, De Morgan duality, disk preservation,
gyro-associativity up to gauge) <em id="S25.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">uniquely</em> determine the central <math id="S25.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(1)</annotation></semantics></math> extension,
i.e. there exists a unique <math id="S25.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> compatible with NGCC/no-signalling stability (no calibration).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S25.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S25.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S25.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S25.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Analytic decay of the geometric tail.</span>
Prove <math id="S25.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{L}\!\oint_{\gamma_{L}}\!A_{\rm geom}=O(L^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>geom</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{L}\!\oint_{\gamma_{L}}\!A_{\rm geom}=O(L^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math> under coarse-graining
on admissible gate families; quantify constants and error terms for CHSH/KCBS/SAT tilings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S25.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S25.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S25.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S25.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spectral formulation.</span>
Express <math id="S25.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm CBL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>CBL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm CBL}</annotation></semantics></math> as a spectral invariant of the exclusivity complex
(e.g. via the non-backtracking operator <math id="S25.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> or normalized Laplacian <math id="S25.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>),
and show <math id="S25.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm CBL}=|\theta_{0}|\,\rho_{\rm face}/(2\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>CBL</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm CBL}=|\theta_{0}|\,\rho_{\rm face}/(2\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S25.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S25.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S25.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S25.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Universality class and gate-law independence.</span>
Classify disk-preserving CBL maps with the same large-<math id="S25.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> intercept; show
gate-law changes move only the <math id="S25.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/L</annotation></semantics></math> slope, not the intercept.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S25.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S25.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S25.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S25.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S25.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–connection exponent.</span>
Establish <math id="S25.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\varepsilon}(L)\sim L^{-\nu_{\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\varepsilon}(L)\sim L^{-\nu_{\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S25.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\varepsilon}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\varepsilon}=1</annotation></semantics></math>
(localized flips on measurement edges) and characterize when <math id="S25.I1.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> differs.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S25.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conjectures.</h5>

<div id="S25.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S25.I2" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S25.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S25.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S25.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S25.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Face-phase uniqueness.</span>
Among central <math id="S25.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(1)</annotation></semantics></math> extensions consistent with NGCC and the flat limit,
there is a unique <math id="S25.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizing a stability margin; calibrated on CHSH it matches <math id="S25.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S25.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S25.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S25.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S25.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spectral equality.</span>
For CBL-inducing complexes, <math id="S25.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm CBL}=\lim_{L\to\infty}\Phi(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\dots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>CBL</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm CBL}=\lim_{L\to\infty}\Phi(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\dots)</annotation></semantics></math>
for a monotone spectral functional <math id="S25.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of gate-law choice.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S25.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S25.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S25.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S25.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RG invariance.</span>
Clause decimation keeps <math id="S25.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm CBL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>CBL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm CBL}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed while contracting <math id="S25.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\rm geom}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>geom</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\rm geom}</annotation></semantics></math>
by exactly one power in length (tail exponent <math id="S25.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<figure id="S25.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Pre-registered Tests (falsification matrix). Each row is a pass/fail check with no
tuning beyond a single CHSH calibration.</figcaption>
<table id="S25.T10.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S25.T10.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S25.T10.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><span id="S25.T10.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Test</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><span id="S25.T10.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Prediction</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;">
<span id="S25.T10.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S25.T10.5.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S25.T10.5.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Fail condition</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S25.T10.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S25.T10.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><span id="S25.T10.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Single–calibration universality</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><math id="S25.T10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}=(\theta_{0}/2\pi)\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">face</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}=(\theta_{0}/2\pi)\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S25.T10.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> on KCBS/SAT/mixes</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;">
<span id="S25.T10.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S25.T10.5.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S25.T10.5.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Intercept drifts beyond finite-size error.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S25.T10.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S25.T10.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><span id="S25.T10.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Gate-law swap</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><span id="S25.T10.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Intercept unchanged; <math id="S25.T10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/L</annotation></semantics></math> slope may change</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;">
<span id="S25.T10.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S25.T10.5.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S25.T10.5.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Intercept depends on gate family.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S25.T10.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S25.T10.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><span id="S25.T10.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Decimation (RG)</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><span id="S25.T10.5.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Intercept unchanged under coarse-graining</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;">
<span id="S25.T10.5.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S25.T10.5.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S25.T10.5.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Intercept changes with decimation.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S25.T10.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S25.T10.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><math id="S25.T10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S25.T10.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">-probe neutrality</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><span id="S25.T10.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Intercept unchanged; slope responds to <math id="S25.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> mask</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;">
<span id="S25.T10.5.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S25.T10.5.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S25.T10.5.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Intercept depends on flip placement.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S25.T10.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S25.T10.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><span id="S25.T10.5.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Orientation parity</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><math id="S25.T10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}(\gamma^{-1})=-\alpha_{\infty}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}(\gamma^{-1})=-\alpha_{\infty}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;">
<span id="S25.T10.5.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S25.T10.5.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S25.T10.5.6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Signs or magnitudes disagree.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S25.T10.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S25.T10.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><span id="S25.T10.5.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mixed faces linearity</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;"><math id="S25.T10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S25.T10.5.7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> linear in <math id="S25.T10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{face}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{face}}</annotation></semantics></math> (blend <math id="S25.T10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="S25.T10.5.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.55pt;padding-bottom:0.55pt;">
<span id="S25.T10.5.7.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S25.T10.5.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S25.T10.5.7.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Nonlinear or inconsistent trend.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S26" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">26 </span>Operational Protocol: Measuring the CBL Constant</h2>

<section id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Goal.</h5>

<div id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a loop family <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\gamma_{L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\gamma_{L}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with known contextual <em id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">face density</em>
<math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\rm face}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\rm face}</annotation></semantics></math> (faces per boundary edge), estimate the large–<math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> intercept
<math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> (signed) of the per-edge holonomy and test the parameter-free
prediction <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}=(\theta_{0}/2\pi)\rho_{\rm face}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}=(\theta_{0}/2\pi)\rho_{\rm face}</annotation></semantics></math> after a <em id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">single</em>
CHSH calibration (Sec. <a href="#S23" title="23 Topological holonomy invariant in CBL ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inputs.</h5>

<div id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(i) A CBL-admissible gate law (disk-preserving, Boolean corners, flat limit);
(ii) a loop family <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\gamma_{L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\gamma_{L}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with computable <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\rm face}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\rm face}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., CHSH: <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/4</annotation></semantics></math>,
KCBS: <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/5</annotation></semantics></math>, SAT variants: <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/6</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2/6</annotation></semantics></math>);
(iii) an orientation convention for signed holonomy.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Output.</h5>

<div id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The signed large–<math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> intercept <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> (per family) and the inferred coupling
<math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm CBL}=|\alpha_{\infty}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>CBL</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm CBL}=|\alpha_{\infty}|</annotation></semantics></math>; pass/fail of the parameter-free prediction.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm5" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 5</span> </span><span id="algorithm5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MeasureCBLConstant<math id="algorithm5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\{\gamma_{L}\},\rho_{\rm face})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\{\gamma_{L}\},\rho_{\rm face})</annotation></semantics></math></span></figcaption>
<div id="algorithm5.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm5.6.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm5.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm5.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Loop family <math id="algorithm5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\gamma_{L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\gamma_{L}\}</annotation></semantics></math>; face density <math id="algorithm5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\rm face}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\rm face}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm5.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span><math id="algorithm5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algorithm5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm CBL}=|\alpha_{\infty}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>CBL</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm CBL}=|\alpha_{\infty}|</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm5.6.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1. Signed per-edge holonomy.</span> For each <math id="algorithm5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> on an increasing grid, compute
<math id="algorithm5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{L}=\frac{1}{L}\oint_{\gamma_{L}}A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{L}=\frac{1}{L}\oint_{\gamma_{L}}A</annotation></semantics></math> with a fixed orientation (sign matters).
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm5.6.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2. Tail fit.</span> Fit <math id="algorithm5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{L}/(2\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{L}/(2\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="algorithm5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/L</annotation></semantics></math> on the largest <math id="algorithm5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>’s to a line
<math id="algorithm5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c/L+\alpha_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c/L+\alpha_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>; record <math id="algorithm5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> and the slope <math id="algorithm5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm5.6.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3. Single calibration (CHSH).</span> On CHSH loops (<math id="algorithm5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\rm face}=1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\rm face}=1/4</annotation></semantics></math>), set
<math id="algorithm5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}^{\rm CHSH}=\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mi>CHSH</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}^{\rm CHSH}=\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> (fine-structure target) and infer
<math id="algorithm5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}=8\pi\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}=8\pi\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm5.6.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4. Parameter-free predictions.</span> For any other family, predict
<math id="algorithm5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}^{\rm pred}=(\theta_{0}/2\pi)\,\rho_{\rm face}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mi>pred</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}^{\rm pred}=(\theta_{0}/2\pi)\,\rho_{\rm face}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm5.6.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5. Test.</span> Measure <math id="algorithm5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> by Step 2 on the new family and check
<math id="algorithm5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}\approx\alpha_{\infty}^{\rm pred}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mi>pred</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}\approx\alpha_{\infty}^{\rm pred}</annotation></semantics></math> within finite-size error.
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm5.6.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6. Report.</span> Report <math id="algorithm5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\rho_{\rm face},\alpha_{\infty},c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\rho_{\rm face},\alpha_{\infty},c)</annotation></semantics></math> per family and pass/fail.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Control checks (pre-registered).</h5>

<div id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S26.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S26.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S26.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S26.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S26.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gate-law swap:</span> repeat with an alternative admissible gate family; the
intercept <math id="S26.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> must be unchanged (slope <math id="S26.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> may vary).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S26.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S26.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S26.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S26.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decimation (RG):</span> coarse-grain <math id="S26.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{L}\!\mapsto\!\gamma_{L/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{L}\!\mapsto\!\gamma_{L/2}</annotation></semantics></math>; the
intercept must be invariant, while <math id="S26.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|c|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|c|</annotation></semantics></math> decreases.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S26.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S26.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S26.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S26.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S26.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–probe neutrality:</span> move localized flips among measurement
edges; the intercept must be unchanged, only <math id="S26.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> changes.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S26.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S26.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S26.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S26.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Orientation parity:</span> reversing the loop orientation flips the sign:
<math id="S26.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}(\gamma^{-1})=-\alpha_{\infty}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}(\gamma^{-1})=-\alpha_{\infty}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S26.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\alpha_{\infty}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\alpha_{\infty}|</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reporting template.</h5>

<div id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each family <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> list <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\rho_{\rm face}^{F},\ \alpha_{\infty}^{F},\ \alpha_{\infty}^{F,\rm pred},\ c^{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi><mi>F</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mi>F</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>pred</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>F</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\rho_{\rm face}^{F},\ \alpha_{\infty}^{F},\ \alpha_{\infty}^{F,\rm pred},\ c^{F})</annotation></semantics></math> and declare <em id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">pass</em> if <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\alpha_{\infty}^{F}-\alpha_{\infty}^{F,\rm pred}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mi>F</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>pred</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\alpha_{\infty}^{F}-\alpha_{\infty}^{F,\rm pred}|</annotation></semantics></math> is within the
tail-fit uncertainty. Mixed tilings (e.g. CHSH/KCBS with fraction <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>) should follow the
linear law <math id="S26.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\infty}(p)=(\theta_{0}/2\pi)\big(p/4+(1-p)/5\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\infty}(p)=(\theta_{0}/2\pi)\big(p/4+(1-p)/5\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S27" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">27 </span>Discussion</h2>

<section id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">CBL coupling and invariance.</h5>

<div id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sec. <a href="#S23.SS1" title="23.1 Holonomy decomposition ‣ 23 Topological holonomy invariant in CBL ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23.1</span></a> argues that the large–<math id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> per-edge holonomy in CBL splits into
a geometric <math id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/L)</annotation></semantics></math> tail plus a size-independent topological term equal to a fixed
phase per contextual face, yielding the dimensionless coupling
<math id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{CBL}}=|\theta_{0}|\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}}/(2\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>CBL</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{CBL}}=|\theta_{0}|\,\rho_{\mathrm{face}}/(2\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>.
After a single CHSH calibration, this produces parameter-free predictions across KCBS
and SAT tilings that match our numerics (Fig. <a href="#S17.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ 17.4 Example 3 — Power and Robustness Grid ‣ 17 Figure Standards and Visualization Protocol ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, Tab. <a href="#A2.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ B.1 Families (CHSH, KCBS, SAT 1/6, SAT 2/6) ‣ Appendix B Toy benchmark generator ‣ Curved Boolean Logic: A Contextual Generalization of Propositional Logic with Algorithmic Consequences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).
The observed invariance of the fitted intercepts under gate-law swap, decimation, and
<math id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-probe placement supports interpreting <math id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{CBL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>CBL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{CBL}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a genuine
topological invariant rather than a modelling artefact.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Practical operators.</h5>

<div id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CBL’s value here is operational: <span id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CBL-AC</span> and <span id="S27.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CBL-CONS</span> are trivial
to add to existing solvers, cost essentially nothing on flat families, and yield
strictly stronger pruning or earlier infeasibility when curved cores are present.
The case studies demonstrate this on SAT, CSP/AC, and 3-Colorability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S27.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Syntax–semantics duality</h3>

<div id="S27.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CBL highlights a clear duality:</p>
<ul id="S27.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S27.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S27.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S27.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Syntax:</span> context-sequent calculus with overlap rules, capturing derivability.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S27.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S27.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S27.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Semantics:</span> presheaf and hypergraph models, capturing obstruction to global sections.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S27.SSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Flat-limit theorems ensure they coincide when <math id="S27.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Curved cases mark divergence: syntactic derivations exist locally, but semantics forbids a global valuation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2</span></span><span id="Thmremark2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Categorical semantics)<span id="Thmremark2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CBL instances can be regarded as presheaves on the context poset <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Ctx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖢𝗍𝗑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Ctx}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Logic of local sections embeds in the topos of presheaves <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Set}^{\mathsf{Ctx}^{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐒𝐞𝐭</mi><msup><mi>𝖢𝗍𝗑</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Set}^{\mathsf{Ctx}^{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Curvature corresponds to failure of global sections functor to be exact.
This connects CBL to categorical logic and topos-theoretic semantics.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3</span></span><span id="Thmremark3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Analogy to algebraic geometry)<span id="Thmremark3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Flat instances correspond to Boolean varieties where global solutions exist.
Curved instances resemble inconsistent polynomial systems: each patch has solutions,
but no global solution exists.
Curvature plays the role of obstruction classes, akin to ideals with no common zero.
This analogy ties logical curvature to algebraic obstructions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S27.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Philosophical implications</h3>

<div id="S27.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Traditionally, mathematics provides tools for physics.
Here, physics (contextuality experiments) revealed incompleteness of Boolean logic.
This makes mathematics partly a science of discovery: structures latent in logic were uncovered by empirical anomalies.
CBL thus blurs lines between mathematics and physics, supporting the view that logics themselves can be discovered experimentally.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S27.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Interdisciplinary links</h3>

<div id="S27.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CBL intersects multiple fields:</p>
<ul id="S27.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S27.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S27.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S27.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Logic and proof theory:</span> extends Gentzen-style systems with overlaps.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S27.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S27.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S27.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Category theory:</span> presheaf/topos models.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S27.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S27.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S27.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theoretical CS:</span> situates within CSP complexity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S27.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S27.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S27.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Foundations of physics:</span> contextuality as source of curvature.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S27.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S27.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S27.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S27.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AI:</span> links to constraint learning and reasoning under inconsistency.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S28" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">28 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<section id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reader takeaways.</h5>

<div id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S28.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S28.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S28.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S28.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Boolean logic is the flat limit; CBL extends it with curvature.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S28.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S28.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S28.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Curvature captures global obstruction despite local classical reasoning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S28.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S28.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S28.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S28.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CBL-SAT</span> is NP-complete, but structure enables pruning in practice.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S28.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S28.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S28.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proof calculus is sound and conservative in the flat limit.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S28.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S28.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S28.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Applications span SAT/CSP, AI/ML, verification, and cryptography.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Synthesis.</h5>

<div id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CBL unifies contextuality research into a logical framework with computational relevance.
It generalizes Boolean logic as relativity generalizes classical mechanics:
the flat case is a special instance of a broader curved structure.
We provided semantics, a proof calculus, a satisfiability formulation,
and solver prototypes demonstrating structural pruning.</p>
</div>
<div id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">
<span id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Main contributions.</span></span>
<span id="S28.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="S28.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S28.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="S28.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Introduced CBL as a generalization of propositional logic.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S28.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S28.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="S28.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Provided equivalent semantics (sheaf, hypergraph, cohomology).</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S28.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S28.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="S28.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Defined a context-sequent proof calculus with overlap rules and flat-limit conservativity.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S28.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S28.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="S28.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Formalized <span id="S28.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CBL-SAT</span>, analyzed complexity and tractability, defined curved cores.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S28.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S28.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="S28.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Developed curvature-aware solver prototypes.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="S28.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S28.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S28.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Illustrated applications across SAT, ML, verification, cryptography.</span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Limitations.</h5>

<div id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CBL does not change asymptotic hardness: <span id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CBL-SAT</span> remains NP-complete.
Its contribution is structural pruning and explanatory clarity.
Benchmarks so far are synthetic; industrial-scale evaluation is future work.
Curvature measures are not unique: cohomological and graph-theoretic variants may differ.
CBL complements but does not replace classical SAT/CSP theory.</p>
</div>
<div id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">
<span id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:293.3pt;">
<span id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Limitations and scope.</span>
CBL is not a polynomial-time solution to SAT.
Advantages lie in pruning and structure, not exponential speedup.
Empirical validation is pending.</span>
</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Outlook.</h5>

<div id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S28.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CBL opens new questions in proof theory (cut elimination in curved cases),
complexity (parameterized algorithms, curvature monotones),
and applications (ML reasoning, verification, cryptography).
It reframes contextuality as a structural logical resource accessible to classical computation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S29" class="ltx_section">
