<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Teaching note</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suggested graduate module:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lecture 1: Boolean logic, SAT, CSP.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lecture 2: Contextuality (Kochen–Specker, KCBS).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lecture 3: CBL semantics, curved cores.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lecture 4: Proof calculus, CBL-SAT.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lab: implement overlaps in a CDCL solver.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Outreach and education</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CBL can be taught with interactive demos.
Undergraduates: small curved examples (3–5 variables).
Graduates: connect logic, complexity, and physics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Glossary of key terms</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<dl id="A5.I1" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="A5.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Context</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A5.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Subset of variables <math id="A5.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A5.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Local valuation</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A5.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assignment within a context.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A5.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Global valuation</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A5.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assignment on <math id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> consistent with all overlaps.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A5.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Curvature</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A5.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Failure of compatible locals to extend globally.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A5.I1.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Curved core</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A5.I1.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Minimal subfamily causing <math id="A5.I1.ix5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A5.I1.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CBL-SAT</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A5.I1.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Decision problem of satisfiability under overlaps.</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Notation and symbols</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We collect recurring symbols. Scalars italic (<math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>), vectors bold (<math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>), sets calligraphic (<math id="A6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T14" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A6.T14.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 14</span>: </span><span id="A6.T14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Core notation.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A6.T14.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A6.T14.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Symbol</td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Meaning</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A6.T14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Set/lattice of measurement contexts</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.T14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Exclusivity graph; vertices <math id="A6.T14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, exclusivity edges <math id="A6.T14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.T14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Curvature/overlap parameter (contextual tension)</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.T14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Canonical phase/turning parameter for a curved face</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.T14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{face}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>face</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{face}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Face density/weight in a folded statistic</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.T14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Face or witness statistic; <math id="A6.T14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> its extremum under CBL</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.T14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Flip probability (perturbation strength)</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.T14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Admissible perturbation budget (Axiom A2)</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.T14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dS/dp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dS/dp</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Local sensitivity of <math id="A6.T14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to infinitesimal flips</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.T14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{S}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Empirical estimate of <math id="A6.T14.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.T14.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Fold}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖥𝗈𝗅𝖽</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Fold}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Folding with window size <math id="A6.T14.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T14.5.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T14.5.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="A6.T14.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{BH}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>BH</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{BH}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T14.5.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Benjamini–Hochberg FDR control at level <math id="A6.T14.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>FAQ</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Is CBL-SAT easier than SAT?</span> No, it is NP-complete. Gains are structural.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Does CBL need quantum hardware?</span> No. Entirely classical.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Is curvature unique?</span> Multiple functionals exist; cohomology rank is canonical.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">What if <math id="A7.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=0</annotation></semantics></math>?</span> Then CBL reduces to SAT.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Why not paraconsistent logic?</span> CBL preserves local classicality, marks obstructions structurally.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
